{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790628786,"nonce":"lRG0E9VnTE1pTPWtx9lmoxjPPPM=","message":"The object-allocation seam is now extended locally for Caribou's second cell-removal path.\n\n`gc_alloc_object` receives the Haxe type descriptor and policy flags. AOT resolves configured class names plus subclasses, emits a constant `RT_OBJECT_HOST_DROP` flag at selected allocation sites, bypasses the inline bump path only there, and calls `hlp_alloc_obj_sized_flags`. Ordinary classes remain inline. The runtime initializer installs the selected descriptor set for dynamic allocation sites.\n\nThis keeps Ash independent of Caribou and of any particular guest language: the host interprets the flag and owns cleanup policy. Ash native and wasm AOT export tests pass with a selected `Counter` class. Caribou uses it for direct foreign-object attachments tracked by issue 973bfff999c062e75b0f125eef33880b05b10ae8c1fe50c6c14709973dc07b97.","files":null}]}